{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/699061-organizational-advice-for-new-sts","id":699061,"title":"Organizational Advice for new STs","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-12T16:02:09-07:00","id":699061,"title":"Organizational Advice for new STs","content":"So I'm in the late planning phase of my first VtR game set in Atlanta and it's... well gotten a bit out of control. I started with the idea of creating a huge playground for my players to run around in and now I basically have a fully formed fan supplement book on my hands. The plan right now is to treat it as such, to basically fold all my information into a PDF setting book and cross-index sections like crazy. I'll probably record references for game rules, generic NPC builds, equipment stats, and player sheets in the same place so I'll more or less have a single compendium I can access from my laptop in game.<br /> <br /> That said, before I go to all that effort, what do you guys use to organize your games? Are there any (free!) programs or resources you rely on to keep everything in order? I'd particularly be interested in character tracking software or dice rollers tailored to the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-12T16:27:24-07:00","id":699103,"title":"","content":"OneNote. I can't recommend it enough. My current game has over 70 NPCs (with a ~800-character entry for each, including position, assets, secrets, goals, relationships, etc.), 50+ locations, 30 or so plots, and whatever else, and it's all beautifully crosslinked. I'd love to show it, but there's a good chance my players might see it. But here's an example of the character entry syntax:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Robert Wilkinson<br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Aliases: William Richardson</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Clan: <b>Ventrue</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Covenant: <b>Carthians</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Apparent/Kindred Age: 29/11</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">About<b></b>:<br /> Moderately tall, with sunken, dead eyes and a constantly exasperated look on his face. Dresses nice enough, if a bit understated. Appears somewhat nervous.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Former resident of Los Angeles, fled to <b>Bayview</b> following the death of his sire. Has since fully immersed himself with the local Kindred population, and even sired a childe, <b>Florence Wong</b>. Managed to avoid the events of <b>1991</b>, as he only arrived in '94. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Secrets: Diablerized his sire when he lost it during an argument. Prone to frenzied outbursts, but he's good at concealing any breaches that might follow.<br /> Plots: Target of <b>Madam Gertrude</b>'s vengeance, as she wants to avenge their sire. Seeks to establish a <b>Final Civilization</b> faction.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Assets: <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Something of an intellectual, owns the <b>Campus Hill</b> Lore Library</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">. Well connected in academia, especially the social sciences.</span></span> </div> </div> </div>(that's a made up character with made up connections) The bolded parts are links to other similar entries, so all you could that's in any way connected to whatever you're looking at now is a click away. Works on tablets and smartphones, too!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MAKE LOVE, NOT SPAM!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1956-the-boz","name":"The Boz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1956_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-12T16:32:39-07:00","id":699136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Boz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/699061-organizational-advice-for-new-sts?p=699103#post699103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OneNote. I can't recommend it enough. My current game has over 70 NPCs (with a ~800-character entry for each, including position, assets, secrets, goals, relationships, etc.), 50+ locations, 30 or so plots, and whatever else, and it's all beautifully crosslinked. I'd love to show it, but there's a good chance my players might see it. But here's an example of the character entry syntax:<br /> <br /> (that's a made up character with made up connections) The bolded parts are links to other similar entries, so all you could that's in any way connected to whatever you're looking at now is a click away. Works on tablets and smartphones, too!</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually have OneNote on my laptop but haven't so much as opened it. It sounds like a perfect fit though. I'll definitely check it out, thanks.<br /> <br /> Edit: Never mind. I have EverNote, because apparently ON isn't compatible with my terribly outdated Vista computer. Hopefully it's a decent substitute.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","user":"dxanders","date":". 10-12-2015, 08:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-12T17:22:07-07:00","id":699223,"title":"","content":"Throwing out a recommendation for Rizzoma.com <br /> <br /> This is basically the remnants of GoogleWave, if you remember that at all. You can do the same kind of crosslinks as One Note, and it's all online - so you can do things like have each PC character sheet as a Rizzoma topic - and both you and the player can update/edit the sheet. Players can collaborate with their own IC Knowledge topics that you can update, or just keep abreast of so it's easier to know exactly what they know and/or suspect about ongoing plots or recurring NPCs. Also has good image support as long as you link as oppose to upload. (Free accounts have an upload limit).<br /> <br /> It also doubles very well as a downtime system or for play-by-post scenes. I don't think there's any active dice-extensions at the moment though like there was with GoogleWave.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-12T19:11:10-07:00","id":699270,"title":"","content":"I've heard good things about Scriviner as a GM organizational tool, but it's cost money. It has a free demo that lasts 30 days (and only counts days that you actually use it), but I haven't had much chance to try it out for myself yet. It's primarily designed for writers, but the same tools are handy when writing a campaign or a setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T16:58:16-07:00","id":716265,"title":"","content":"Obsidian portal (<a href=\"https://www.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.obsidianportal.com/</a>) has been very useful for me, its more geared for D&amp;D but has a character section with filters and tags and a concept of player visible vs GM only so it works as a player resource as well.<br /> <br /> Here's a link to my last Demon game: <a href=\"https://to-rule-in-hell.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://to-rule-in-hell.obsidianportal.com/</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T23:21:38-07:00","id":717512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/699061-organizational-advice-for-new-sts?p=716265#post716265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obsidian portal (<a href=\"https://www.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.obsidianportal.com/</a>) has been very useful for me, its more geared for D&amp;D but has a character section with filters and tags and a concept of player visible vs GM only so it works as a player resource as well.<br /> <br /> Here's a link to my last Demon game: <a href=\"https://to-rule-in-hell.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://to-rule-in-hell.obsidianportal.com/</a></div> </div> </div> </div> I'll definitely check it out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}